  "title": "1992 whites-only referendum on negotiations",
  "summary": "On 17 March 1992 South Africa's white voters were asked in a referendum called by President F. W. de Klerk whether to continue negotiating an end to apartheid with the ANC and other formerly banned groups. About 69 percent voted yes, giving him a mandate for negotiations.",
